{"world_id":"wld_tidal_conservatories","title":"The Glass Tide","logline":"When junior tide-warden Mara Ilek discovers the Glassgate Locks are silting shut ahead of schedule, she must persuade a proud glassblower master and win a wary barge pilot's help to pause the firing season and dredge before the spring tide fails the city.","theme":"Proof matters most when people share the work and the cost.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"A Shallowing Channel","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mara_finds_silt","title":"The Sounding Line","summary":"At the Glassgate Locks, Mara's sounding poles show the sills filling weeks ahead of the tide tables. She records the settle lines carefully, but worries that raising the alarm will make her sound like her mother.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Confirm whether the gates are silting early enough to threaten the spring tide.","conflict":"Mara trusts her measurements but fears the guilds will dismiss her as an alarmist.","outcome":"The soundings confirm an early buildup; Mara has clear evidence but delays taking it beyond the wardens.","depends_on":[]},{"id":"scn_pell_sets_calendar","title":"The Full Firing Season","summary":"At Bellmaker's Quay, Oren sets the guild's firing calendar and insists the locks stay open through the full season. He has read the tide tables, but refuses to reconsider a schedule his workers depend on.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Keep the locks open through the full firing season.","conflict":"The tide tables already hint at risk, but Oren cannot admit a trade-off once he has committed to the calendar.","outcome":"The guild begins preparations for a full season, making an early dredging closure harder to win.","depends_on":[]},{"id":"scn_mara_holds_back","title":"A Note Unsent","summary":"Mara compares her latest measurements with the notes she keeps in her mother's hand. Certain of the pattern, she still waits for more proof before going to the guilds.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Prepare a case strong enough to persuade the guild masters.","conflict":"Mara assumes the soundings will speak for themselves and lets fear of her mother's reputation keep her quiet.","outcome":"Her delay gives the guild preparations time to advance while she seeks corroboration.","depends_on":["scn_mara_finds_silt","scn_pell_sets_calendar"]}]},{"id":"act_rising_action","title":"Evidence and Terms","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mara_hires_sana","title":"A Bargain for the Channel","summary":"Mara asks Sana to take a barge through the gate channels and verify the shallow readings. Sana agrees, but makes clear that the cooperative will not surrender its claim to dredged silt.","location_id":"loc_algae_fields","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Secure an independent channel survey before confronting the guilds.","conflict":"Sana wants fair pay and a say in silt ownership; Mara needs her help but has no authority to promise away the wardens' charter.","outcome":"They agree to survey together, with Sana's silt-rights demand still unresolved.","depends_on":["scn_mara_holds_back"]},{"id":"scn_sana_confirms_depth","title":"The Tiller's Answer","summary":"Sana pilots the barge along the gate channels while Mara takes fresh soundings. The tiller catches in unexpectedly shallow water, and both methods point to the same early silting.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Verify the channel depth and establish how urgently dredging must begin.","conflict":"The channel is difficult to read, and Sana needs assurance that the cooperative will not lose its silt rights if it helps.","outcome":"The independent check confirms the danger; Sana agrees to stand behind the evidence if the silt dispute is addressed openly.","depends_on":["scn_mara_hires_sana"]},{"id":"scn_pell_rejects_evidence","title":"Tables at the Quay","summary":"Mara presents the paired measurements to Oren at Bellmaker's Quay. He recognizes the warning in the tide tables but dismisses the soundings as insufficient grounds to cut short the season.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Persuade Oren to pause the firing season and schedule an early gate closure.","conflict":"Oren fears the cost to his guild's families and, unwilling to concede a trade-off, treats corroborating evidence as a challenge to his authority.","outcome":"Oren refuses the closure, but Sana's testimony makes it harder for him to dismiss Mara's warning as apprentice work.","depends_on":["scn_sana_confirms_depth"]},{"id":"scn_silt_rights_terms","title":"Who Owns the Silt","summary":"At the Mangrove Terraces, Mara and Sana work through what dredging would mean under the silt-debt rule: the dredgers own the fertile silt but must spread it on the terraces within a season. Sana presses for the cooperative's claim to be respected.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Agree on terms that let the cooperative dredge without giving up its silt rights.","conflict":"Sana distrusts the wardens' charter, while Mara cannot promise that the guilds will accept a closure or that the cooperative will get its way.","outcome":"Sana agrees to risk her barge on the survey and present the silt terms alongside the evidence.","depends_on":["scn_pell_rejects_evidence"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Gate Decision","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_guild_hall_decision","title":"A Season Cut Short","summary":"Mara and Sana return to Bellmaker's Quay with the matched readings and the proposed silt terms. Oren sees that the tide tables and the channel both tell the same story; after resisting the cost, he chooses to shorten the firing season rather than risk losing the tide that sustains it.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Win agreement to close the gates and begin dredging before the spring tide.","conflict":"Oren must put the lagoon's survival ahead of the full season he promised, while Sana requires that the cooperative's silt rights be honored.","outcome":"Oren agrees to halt firing for the closure, and Sana commits the barge; the immediate dispute becomes a shared plan.","depends_on":["scn_silt_rights_terms"]},{"id":"scn_dredge_before_spring","title":"The Locks Shut","summary":"With the guild's firing paused, Mara coordinates the gate closure and Sana pilots the barge through the shallow channel as dredging begins. Oren leaves the quay to help organize his guild's workers for the interrupted season.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Clear the sills before the spring tide arrives.","conflict":"The channel is already shallow, the deadline is close, and the guild's lost firing time makes every hour of closure contentious.","outcome":"The crew clears the immediate buildup in time for the spring tide to enter through the gates.","depends_on":["scn_guild_hall_decision"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"A Shared Channel","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silt_spread","title":"The Terrace Share","summary":"After the dredging, Sana's cooperative hauls the recovered fertile silt to the Mangrove Terraces and spreads it within the season. The wardens honor the cooperative's claim, and the terraces gain the soil the rules require them to receive.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Fulfill the silt-debt rule while ensuring the cooperative receives its due.","conflict":"The work must serve the terraces without erasing the cooperative's rights or the labor that made the dredging possible.","outcome":"The silt is shared as agreed, and Sana's risk earns the cooperative a fair place in the city's recovery.","depends_on":["scn_dredge_before_spring"]},{"id":"scn_shortened_season","title":"A Different Calendar","summary":"At Bellmaker's Quay, Oren sets a shorter firing calendar and acknowledges that the guild's work depends on a healthy lagoon. Mara brings the new soundings to the guilds herself, inviting them to share responsibility for watching the gates.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Establish a workable firing schedule and make early warnings part of the guilds' decisions.","conflict":"The shortened season still costs the guild, and Mara must replace solitary proof with the shared responsibility she once feared asking for.","outcome":"Oren accepts the cost of the interrupted season, while Mara steps forward as a warden whose evidence can bring others into action.","depends_on":["scn_silt_spread"]}]}]}
