{"world_id":"wld_underworld_ledger","title":"The Last Audit","logline":"When junior scribe Itho Pel discovers a newly arrived soul miscast in the wrong ledger column, he must persuade the weigher who certified the error and an oath-bound archivist to supply the three keys for a correction before the soul is sent to the Erasure Wells.","theme":"A just record needs more than accurate ink; it needs people willing to answer for it.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"A Column Out of Place","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_itho_spots_miscast","title":"The Wrong Column","summary":"While transcribing the latest arrivals in the Counting Halls, Itho's fault-sight catches a mortal soul's deeds entered under the wrong column. The arriving soul's tally-slip confirms the discrepancy, but the copied ledger is already moving toward the scales.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Identify the miscast entry and stop it from being treated as a settled account.","conflict":"Itho trusts the written columns over his seniors' assurances, and his blunt insistence makes the clerks regard him as a troublemaker.","outcome":"He confirms the error against the tally-slip and learns that only a three-key correction can change the account before weighing."},{"id":"scn_ors_refuses_audit","title":"The Seal at the Scales","summary":"Itho carries the discrepancy to Dame Ors at the Hall of Scales. Ors recognizes the column as wrong but calls the error small and orders the soul weighed as written.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Get Ors to halt the weighing and authorize an audit.","conflict":"Ors wants to protect the weighers' infallibility, while Itho's accusation would put her certification beside the miscast.","outcome":"Ors refuses the audit and bars Itho from the scales; the soul remains queued, but the weighing is imminent.","depends_on":["scn_itho_spots_miscast"]}]},{"id":"act_rising_action","title":"Three Keys Required","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_itho_seeks_warrant","title":"A Warrant for the Stacks","summary":"Itho seeks Ors again, this time asking for the weigher's warrant needed to access the matching sealed ledger in the Lamp Archive. Ors refuses and orders him to stop pursuing the account.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Obtain a warrant that will let the audit compare the current entry with the archive record.","conflict":"Ors's stated goal is to weigh the soul as written, and Itho's insistence only strengthens her resolve to quash the audit.","outcome":"Itho leaves without a warrant and must ask Hemo to locate the ledger without opening it.","depends_on":["scn_ors_refuses_audit"]},{"id":"scn_hemo_finds_index","title":"The Unopened Index","summary":"At the Lamp Archive, Hemo uses his memory of the stacks' cross-references to identify the matching ledger and folio without reading a sealed page. He will not open it without a weigher's warrant.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Find the archival account that can corroborate Itho's correction.","conflict":"Hemo wants the archive kept honest but fears losing his lamp and post if he breaks the rules; Itho demands proof as if Hemo's caution were just another bad entry.","outcome":"Hemo identifies the exact folio but refuses to retrieve it without authorization, leaving Itho with a clear request for Ors.","depends_on":["scn_itho_seeks_warrant"]},{"id":"scn_itho_owns_his_bluntness","title":"People Behind the Ink","summary":"Itho returns to the Counting Halls to prepare a formal correction rather than dismissing Hemo's caution as mere procedure. He states plainly that the record is wrong, then adds the names and seals that must answer for it.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Make a correction request that addresses both the evidence and the risks facing its signatories.","conflict":"Itho's habit of trusting ink more than people has damaged Hemo's trust, and a perfect form cannot compel anyone to sign.","outcome":"Itho acknowledges Hemo's stake and prepares a request for the archive folio, giving Hemo reason to keep helping without breaking his oath.","depends_on":["scn_hemo_finds_index"]},{"id":"scn_ors_detects_balance","title":"The Weight of a Signature","summary":"At the Hall of Scales, Ors uses her scale-craft to test the queued soul against the account. The balance confirms what she already suspected: the written column cannot be reconciled with the soul's weight.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Weigh the soul as written and preserve the authority of her certification.","conflict":"Ors's own ability exposes the contradiction, while admitting it would attach her seal to the error she helped certify.","outcome":"She delays the weighing rather than certify a false balance, buying Itho time but still withholding the archive warrant.","depends_on":["scn_itho_owns_his_bluntness"]},{"id":"scn_ors_grants_warrant","title":"An Uncomfortable Warrant","summary":"Itho presents the tally-slip, the prepared correction, and Ors's own scale reading. Ors admits the column is wrong but insists that the audit must establish exactly how the account was miscast.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Secure Ors's warrant so Hemo can retrieve the matching archive folio.","conflict":"Ors fears that an audit will expose her certification, while Itho needs her authority rather than another unsupported accusation.","outcome":"Ors grants a narrow warrant, placing her seal on the audit and making the archive record accessible.","depends_on":["scn_ors_detects_balance"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Correction","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hemo_retrieves_folio","title":"The Sealed Page",