n","title":"Three Keys Required","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_itho_seeks_warrant","title":"A Warrant for the Stacks","summary":"Itho seeks Ors again, this time asking for the weigher's warrant needed to access the matching sealed ledger in the Lamp Archive. Ors refuses and orders him to stop pursuing the account.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Obtain a warrant that will let the audit compare the current entry with the archive record.","conflict":"Ors's stated goal is to weigh the soul as written, and Itho's insistence only strengthens her resolve to quash the audit.","outcome":"Itho leaves without a warrant and must ask Hemo to locate the ledger without opening it.","depends_on":["scn_ors_refuses_audit"]},{"id":"scn_hemo_finds_index","title":"The Unopened Index","summary":"At the Lamp Archive, Hemo uses his memory of the stacks' cross-references to identify the matching ledger and folio without reading a sealed page. He will not open it without a weigher's warrant.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Find the archival account that can corroborate Itho's correction.","conflict":"Hemo wants the archive kept honest but fears losing his lamp and post if he breaks the rules; Itho demands proof as if Hemo's caution were just another bad entry.","outcome":"Hemo identifies the exact folio but refuses to retrieve it without authorization, leaving Itho with a clear request for Ors.","depends_on":["scn_itho_seeks_warrant"]},{"id":"scn_itho_owns_his_bluntness","title":"People Behind the Ink","summary":"Itho returns to the Counting Halls to prepare a formal correction rather than dismissing Hemo's caution as mere procedure. He states plainly that the record is wrong, then adds the names and seals that must answer for it.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Make a correction request that addresses both the evidence and the risks facing its signatories.","conflict":"Itho's habit of trusting ink more than people has damaged Hemo's trust, and a perfect form cannot compel anyone to sign.","outcome":"Itho acknowledges Hemo's stake and prepares a request for the archive folio, giving Hemo reason to keep helping without breaking his oath.","depends_on":["scn_hemo_finds_index"]},{"id":"scn_ors_detects_balance","title":"The Weight of a Signature","summary":"At the Hall of Scales, Ors uses her scale-craft to test the queued soul against the account. The balance confirms what she already suspected: the written column cannot be reconciled with the soul's weight.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Weigh the soul as written and preserve the authority of her certification.","conflict":"Ors's own ability exposes the contradiction, while admitting it would attach her seal to the error she helped certify.","outcome":"She delays the weighing rather than certify a false balance, buying Itho time but still withholding the archive warrant.","depends_on":["scn_itho_owns_his_bluntness"]},{"id":"scn_ors_grants_warrant","title":"An Uncomfortable Warrant","summary":"Itho presents the tally-slip, the prepared correction, and Ors's own scale reading. Ors admits the column is wrong but insists that the audit must establish exactly how the account was miscast.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Secure Ors's warrant so Hemo can retrieve the matching archive folio.","conflict":"Ors fears that an audit will expose her certification, while Itho needs her authority rather than another unsupported accusation.","outcome":"Ors grants a narrow warrant, placing her seal on the audit and making the archive record accessible.","depends_on":["scn_ors_detects_balance"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Correction","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hemo_retrieves_folio","title":"The Sealed Page",