n","title":"Three Keys Required","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_itho_seeks_warrant","title":"A Warrant for the Stacks","summary":"Itho seeks Ors again, this time asking for the weigher's warrant needed to access the matching sealed ledger in the Lamp Archive. Ors refuses and orders him to stop pursuing the account.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Obtain a warrant that will let the audit compare the current entry with the archive record.","conflict":"Ors's stated goal is to weigh the soul as written, and Itho's insistence only strengthens her resolve to quash the audit.","outcome":"Itho leaves without a warrant and must ask Hemo to locate the ledger without opening it.","depends_on":["scn_ors_refuses_audit"]},{"id":"scn_hemo_finds_index","title":"The Unopened Index","summary":"At the Lamp Archive, Hemo uses his memory of the stacks' cross-references to identify the matching ledger and folio without reading a sealed page. He will not open it without a weigher's warrant.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Find the archival account that can corroborate Itho's correction.","conflict":"Hemo wants the archive kept honest but fears losing his lamp and post if he breaks the rules; Itho demands proof as if Hemo's caution were just another bad entry.","outcome":"Hemo identifies the exact folio but refuses to retrieve it without authorization, leaving Itho with a clear request for Ors.","depends_on":["scn_itho_seeks_warrant"]},{"id":"scn_itho_owns_his_bluntness","title":"People Behind the Ink","summary":"Itho returns to the Counting Halls to prepare a formal correction rather than dismissing Hemo's caution as mere procedure. He states plainly that the record is wrong, then adds the names and seals that must answer for it.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Make a correction request that addresses both the evidence and the risks facing its signatories.","conflict":"Itho's habit of trusting ink more than people has damaged Hemo's trust, and a perfect form cannot compel anyone to sign.","outcome":"Itho acknowledges Hemo's stake and prepares a request for the archive folio, giving Hemo reason to keep helping without breaking his oath.","depends_on":["scn_hemo_finds_index"]},{"id":"scn_ors_detects_balance","title":"The Weight of a Signature","summary":"At the Hall of Scales, Ors uses her scale-craft to test the queued soul against the account. The balance confirms what she already suspected: the written column cannot be reconciled with the soul's weight.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Weigh the soul as written and preserve the authority of her certification.","conflict":"Ors's own ability exposes the contradiction, while admitting it would attach her seal to the error she helped certify.","outcome":"She delays the weighing rather than certify a false balance, buying Itho time but still withholding the archive warrant.","depends_on":["scn_itho_owns_his_bluntness"]},{"id":"scn_ors_grants_warrant","title":"An Uncomfortable Warrant","summary":"Itho presents the tally-slip, the prepared correction, and Ors's own scale reading. Ors admits the column is wrong but insists that the audit must establish exactly how the account was miscast.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Secure Ors's warrant so Hemo can retrieve the matching archive folio.","conflict":"Ors fears that an audit will expose her certification, while Itho needs her authority rather than another unsupported accusation.","outcome":"Ors grants a narrow warrant, placing her seal on the audit and making the archive record accessible.","depends_on":["scn_ors_detects_balance"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Correction","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hemo_retrieves_folio","title":"The Sealed Page","summary":"With Ors's warrant, Hemo retrieves the indexed ledger and opens it without reading its sealed page aloud. Itho compares the entry with the tally-slip and identifies where the deeds were entered in the wrong column.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Verify the miscast against the original account without violating Hemo's lamp oath.","conflict":"The page is sealed and Hemo risks his post by assisting, while the approaching weighing leaves little time for a careful comparison.","outcome":"Itho confirms the error from the written record, and Hemo commits to authenticating the archive reference as the third key.","depends_on":["scn_ors_grants_warrant"]},{"id":"scn_three_keys_seal","title":"Three Hands on the Record","summary":"Itho brings the verified correction to the Hall of Scales. Ors must choose whether to sign beside the error she certified; Hemo authenticates the archive reference without reading the sealed page aloud.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Secure the scribe, weigher, and lamplighter keys before the soul is weighed.","conflict":"Ors risks her reputation by admitting the miscast, Hemo risks his position by supporting the audit, and Itho must trust people to complete what his ink alone cannot.","outcome":"Ors signs the correction, Hemo seals the archive reference, and Itho enters the amended account; the three keys make the correction stand before the weighing.","depends_on":["scn_hemo_retrieves_folio"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"A Fair Account","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_soul_weighed_correctly","title":"The Account Holds","summary":"With the corrected ledger in hand, Ors weighs the soul against the amended account. The balance holds, and the soul is allowed to rest rather than sent to the Erasure Wells.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Ensure the soul is weighed against the corrected record.","conflict":"Ors must certify a correction that exposes her earlier failure, while Itho must accept that the process depends on the weigher's judgment as well as his proof.","outcome":"Ors certifies the fair balance; the soul's account is settled without any return to the living.","depends_on":["scn_three_keys_seal"]},{"id":"scn_new_standard","title":"The Next Entry","summary":"Back in the Counting Halls, Itho files the triple-sealed correction, while Hemo keeps his lamp and post because he never read the sealed page aloud. Ors's signature remains attached to the audit, a lasting mark against the claim of infallibility.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Preserve the corrected account and make its chain of responsibility clear.","conflict":"The offices would prefer the error forgotten, but the three signatures make concealment harder and leave each of them accountable.","outcome":"Itho learns that accurate ink requires willing witnesses, Hemo has risked his standing for the archive's honesty, and Ors must live with her seal beside the truth.","depends_on":["scn_soul_weighed_correctly"]}]}]}
